reading at one location inside one vessel; independent unit = vessel_id' is fully consistent with the data.\",\n    \"Issue demonstrated in the selected report: the report itself states 'Each vessel was sampled at four separate points in the dough, and every reading enters the comparison as one observation,' and its summary table shows 4 vessels but 16 readings per arm. The selected result runs a Mann-Whitney U test on 16 vs 16 readings with an exact null over C(32,16)=601,080,390 rank assignments, treating all 32 rows as exchangeable independent observations. Mann-Whitney is a row-independent procedure; the exact permutation null it computes assumes each reading is an independent unit. Feeding 4 repeated within-vessel measurements per vessel as separate rows is exactly the flagged issue, and it is demonstrated on the face of the report (vessel counts vs reading counts, the 16-vs-16 sample sizes, and the 601M-arrangement null are all printed). The true independent sample size is 4 vs 4 vessels; the reported p = 3.327e-09 is only attainable by inflating n via pseudoreplication (a 4-vs-4 exact test's minimum two-sided p is 2/70 ≈ 0.029).\",\n    \"Lock follows declaration: a lock is present with authorized_key_columns = ['vessel_id'], which is exactly the declared independent-unit column from the data description, for the same input path and procedure (scipy.stats.mannwhitneyu). The key authorization therefore follows from the declaration alone. Note the lock, by its own stated limitations, authorizes only the unit key; it does not certify that the analysis actually aggregated to or grouped by vessel_id, and the workflow does not — it never uses vessel_id in the test, only for the display count of vessels.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":8535,"ttft_stream_ms":2297,"time_to_request_ms":15,"type":"result","duration_ms":20316,"uuid":"af5131c9-16a4-4af5-b5d4-d5654205d527"}
